# Tangerine Compiler — Semantic Slices over lowered MIR (audit §33)
# Self-hosting compiler written in Tangerine
#
# Compiler-derived SLICES over the VERIFIED MIR program (the instance the
# compile phases guard with verify_mir — every entry takes a lowered
# MirProgram; no AST/typed/env state is read). A slice is a set of
# statement-level MIR nodes + external anchors as stable key texts — never
# MIR indices, never spans (SliceResult.span_keys are presentation-only
# and never enter slice_digest — the §29 spans-are-metadata protocol).
#
# STATEMENT IDENTITY — MirStatement records carry NO stable id (the only
# MIR ids are the per-function MirLocalId/MirBlockId domains), so nodes
# are indexed DETERMINISTICALLY by (function key, block index, statement
# index) as the audit prescribes:
#   function key = the MirFunction EMISSION NAME (f.name — the only
#     identity the lowered program carries; the snapshot walks use the
#     same text). The stable DEF key text ("path::name#signature")
#     resolves only through the typed program's resolver tables —
#     MirProgram-only slices cannot build it — DOCUMENTED GAP (the §30
#     boundary for IR-synthesized bodies).
#   block index  = MirBlockId.id (deterministic at lowering; passes may
#     DELETE blocks and leave gaps, so ids — never Vec positions).
#   stmt index   = the index in MirBlock.statements; the block TERMINATOR
#     is the block's final node.
#   Statement key text "<fn emission name>#B<block id>#S<stmt index>",
#   terminator key text "<fn emission name>#B<block id>#T". Deterministic
#   per verified program; the digest form rides slice_digest.
#
# THE DEF-USE MODEL:
#   - A VALUE is one local slot (MirLocalId.id — the §33 ValueId
#     adaptation; the mir.tg optimizer's collect_operand_read /
#     collect_rvalue_reads / collect_call_arg_read /
#     collect_terminator_reads helpers all reason in local ids). Local 0
#     is the "_ret" RETURN PLACE (start_function's convention): MirReturn
#     terminators READ local 0 (no statement reads the slot).
#   - READ of a value: operand reads (place roots), MirRef/MirDiscriminant/
#     MirLen places, phi sources, call FUNC operands, and call ARGUMENTS —
#     mirroring collect_call_arg_read VERBATIM: a BARE local passed with
#     the Initialize (set) effect is a WRITE, not a read. A MirDeinit
#     READS the destroyed place (its final use).
#   - DEF of a value: a MirAssign/MirCall whose destination is the BARE
#     local (the write that ENDS a def chain). A projected destination is
#     a PARTIAL DEF: it affects a piece of the value, is included, feeds
#     its operand reads into the chain, but does NOT end it (the aggregate
#     base is defined earlier).
#   - Def-use edge: a use U is fed by the nearest def of the same local
#     scanning BACKWARD over the block's linear order (in-block exact); a
#     use with no def in its block is fed from the PREDECESSOR blocks (a
#     bounded worklist over the CFG — Goto/SwitchInt/Call/Assert/Deinit
#     targets, never a full reaching-def fixed point). MIR is NOT
#     single-assignment: def chains resolve per use, so slice_value seeds
#     one backward walk per use site.
#
# THE FOUR SLICES:
#   slice_value(fn_key, value_id) — the value's def chain (its def, the
#     partial defs affecting it, the defs of every operand those defs read
#     — recursively), resolved from every use site. A value with NO use
#     sites yields the empty slice (documented).
#   slice_statement(fn_key, stmt_key) — the forward use slice of the
#     statement's defs: nodes transitively reading the defined value,
#     forward per block and propagated to SUCCESSOR blocks (a bare
#     redefinition KILLS the chain; partial defs pass through). A def
#     escaping through a call edge records the external anchor
#     "call:<callee emission name>:arg<n>"; a node with no defs yields
#     the empty slice (documented).
#   slice_failure(diag) — the statements contributing to a diagnostic:
#     its primary site maps to a MIR node through the SPAN MAP (below);
#     the result = the FAILURE TRACE (the enclosing block's statements
#     from its head through the mapped node) UNION the anchored def chains
#     of the failing node's read operands (an assert's condition+bounds).
#   slice_effect(class) — one result per function whose DIRECT §11 summary
#     has the class: the class's DIRECT sites (MirCall/MirDeinit
#     terminators whose §11 classification dirties the class —
#     mir_effect_classify_call/_deinit reused verbatim — plus the
#     string-concat MirBinOp::Add assignment and the fail-closed algebraic
#     perform) plus each site's anchored def chains of the values it
#     reads. A class reaching a function only through in-program callees
#     is NOT re-listed: its sites live in the callee's own row.
#
# THE TYPED ENTRY (audit item 22): mir_slice(Option[MirProgram],
# MirSliceRequest) routes ONE kind onto those engines (Failure onto the
# node-anchored slice_failure machinery above) plus the two module-local
# walks: ControlDependence (a bounded CFG-predecessor walk adding the
# conditional terminators that decide the anchor block's reachability —
# the CFG-only slice; the conditions' def chains stay the dataflow kinds'
# business) and Ownership (the nodes whose operand/place keys touch the
# anchor's local/place family — conservative). Request anchors are the §33
# node key texts "<fn emission name>#B<block id>#S<stmt index>" / "#T",
# the §27 local key texts (declared name or the "l<id>" locator), the §7
# place key texts (root + projections over the MIR type table) or the
# effect-class words "alloc" / "block" / "io" — the per-kind grammar and
# the error mapping live at the entry's own doc below.
#
# SPAN MAP (how diagnostics map to statements): every lowered node
# carries its source Span (synthesized nodes carry span_dummy). A
# diagnostic's Option[Span] resolves deterministically over program order
# (functions in MirProgram.functions order, blocks in Vec order,
# statements in index order, then the terminator): tier 1 CONTAINS the
# diagnostic start offset; tier 2 overlaps it; tier 3 the smallest |start
# gap|; file texts compare only when both are non-empty. No
# span-to-statement table exists (presentation-grade); an unmapped
# diagnostic yields the empty result (documented).
#
# BOUNDEDNESS / APPROXIMATIONS (deterministic, documented): at most
# slice_max_items work items per call; a wanted PARAMETER reaching the
# ENTRY block's head records the "param:<index>:<name>" anchor; any other
# never-defined wanted local drops silently; a walk exhausting its budget
# stops adding (the deterministic FIFO-worklist prefix). Control
# dependence is NOT modeled (the failure trace is the only control-flow
# term); Goto/Abort/Unreachable carry no operands and are never reads.
#
# DETERMINISM: bounded worklists process FIFO; every result Vec sorts
# (statements, span keys and externals textually) before leaving the
# module; slice_digest hashes the SORTED canonical JSONL row set (spans
# and digest words never serialize).

use std::collections::{Vec, Map, Set}

use tg_compiler::ids::{StableDigest, stable_digest_of}
use tg_compiler::token::{Span}
use tg_compiler::parser::{Diagnostic}
use tg_compiler::types::{AccessEffect, EffectClass, EffectSummary, effect_class_slot_index, effect_summary_has_class}
use tg_compiler::semantic_model::{semantic_json_escape}
use tg_compiler::mir::{
  MirProgram, MirFunction, MirStatement, MirStatementKind, MirRvalueKind, MirBinOp,
  MirOperand, MirOperandKind, MirConstantKind, MirTerminator, MirTerminatorKind,
  MirTypeDefKind, MirCallArg, MirCallValue, Place, Projection, AssertMessage,
  MirEffectState, mir_effect_scan_function, mir_effect_classify_call,
  mir_effect_classify_deinit, mir_effect_place_type,
  mir_effect_operand_is_string, mir_effect_type_is_string_like
}

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Result record and budgets
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# One slice's result: sorted stable key texts of the included statements,
# sorted external anchors (call edges the defs escape through; parameters
# the def chains end at) and presentation-only span keys ("<stmt key>|<
# file>:<start>-<end>", one per included node with a real span).
struct SliceResult
  function_key: String
  statements: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  external: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  span_keys: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
end

# The empty result (an invalid key, an unmapped span, a no-def slice).
def slice_result_empty() -> SliceResult
  SliceResult {
    function_key: "",
    statements: Vec::new(),
    external: Vec::new(),
    span_keys: Vec::new()
  }
end

# The deterministic cap of every engine below.
def slice_max_items() -> Int
  4096
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Statement-key text helpers (the §33 stable text domain)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# Node keys: statements "#S<idx>"; the terminator "#T" (its index is
# MirBlock.statements.len(), so the spellings never collide).
def slice_stmt_key(name: String, block_id: Int, idx: Int) -> String
  name + "#B" + block_id.to_string() + "#S" + idx.to_string()
end

def slice_term_key(name: String, block_id: Int) -> String
  name + "#B" + block_id.to_string() + "#T"
end

# A fresh copy of a span (field-clone idiom).
def slice_span_copy(sp: Span) -> Span
  Span { file: sp.file.clone(), start: sp.start, end_pos: sp.end_pos }
end

# The presentation span key "<stmt key>|<file>:<start>-<end>" ("" when dummy).
def slice_span_key(node_key: String, span: Span) -> String
  if span.start == 0 && span.end_pos == 0 && span.file.len() == 0 then
    return ""
  end
  node_key + "|" + span.file.clone() + ":" + span.start.to_string() + "-" + span.end_pos.to_string()
end

# Whether a text is all ASCII digits (the key-component validation).
def slice_is_digits(text: String) -> Bool
  if text.len() == 0 then return false end
  var i = 0
  while i < text.len() do
    let ch = text.slice(i, i + 1)
    if ch < "0" || ch > "9" then
      return false
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  true
end

# The deterministic Int parse of a non-empty digit text.
def slice_text_to_int(text: String) -> Int
  var value = 0
  var i = 0
  while i < text.len() do
    let bs = text.slice(i, i + 1).bytes()
    if bs.len() > 0 then
      value = value * 10 + (bs[0] as Int - 48)
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  value
end

# The LAST "#B" marker of a key (-1 when absent; emission names never
# contain "#", so the last marker is the key's).
def slice_key_marker(key: String) -> Int
  var i = key.len() - 2
  while i >= 0 do
    if key.slice(i, i + 2) == "#B" then
      return i
    end
    i = i - 1
  end
  -1
end

# Parse a node key into (block id, node index, is_terminator); the fn prefix
# must equal name; Option::None when malformed.
def slice_key_parts(name: String, key: String) -> Option[(Int, Int, Bool)]
  let mark = slice_key_marker(&key)
  if mark <= 0 then return Option::None end
  if key.slice(0, mark) != name then return Option::None end
  var i = mark + 2
  var block_text = ""
  while i < key.len() do
    let ch = key.slice(i, i + 1)
    if ch == "#" then
      break
    elsif ch < "0" || ch > "9" then
      return Option::None
    end
    block_text = block_text + ch
    i = i + 1
  end
  if block_text.len() == 0 || i >= key.len() then return Option::None end
  if key.slice(i, key.len()) == "#T" then
    return Option::Some((slice_text_to_int(&block_text), -1, true))
  end
  if key.slice(i, i + 2) != "#S" then return Option::None end
  let idx_text = key.slice(i + 2, key.len())
  if !slice_is_digits(&idx_text) then return Option::None end
  Option::Some((slice_text_to_int(&block_text), slice_text_to_int(&idx_text), false))
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Per-function index — the program's node universe, built once per call
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

struct SliceFnCtx
  # the function's emission name (its slice function key).
  name: String
  # the function body.
  f: MirFunction
  # MirBlockId.id -> block Vec index.
  block_of_id: Map[Int, Int]
  # predecessor / successor blocks (their Vec indices) per block Vec idx.
  preds: Map[Int, Vec[Int]]
  succs: Map[Int, Vec[Int]]
end

# The FIRST function's ctx by emission name (first-wins on duplicates);
# Option::None when absent.
def slice_fn_find(mir: MirProgram, name: String) -> Option[SliceFnCtx]
  var found = -1
  var fi = 0
  while fi < mir.functions.len() do
    if mir.functions[fi].name == name then
      found = fi
      break
    end
    fi = fi + 1
  end
  if found < 0 then return Option::None end
  let f = mir.functions[found]
  var block_of_id: Map[Int, Int] = Map::new()
  var preds: Map[Int, Vec[Int]] = Map::new()
  var succs: Map[Int, Vec[Int]] = Map::new()
  var bi = 0
  while bi < f.blocks.len() do
    block_of_id.insert(f.blocks[bi].id.id, bi)
    preds.insert(bi, Vec::new())
    succs.insert(bi, Vec::new())
    bi = bi + 1
  end
  # The CFG edge maps (by Vec index), from the terminator targets (return,
  # abort and unreachable end the flow).
  var pi = 0
  while pi < f.blocks.len() do
    var out_targets: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
    match f.blocks[pi].terminator.kind
    when MirTerminatorKind::MirGoto(target) then out_targets.push(target.id)
    when MirTerminatorKind::MirSwitchInt { op, targets, default_target } then
      for arm in targets do
        out_targets.push(arm.target.id)
      end
      out_targets.push(default_target.id)
    when MirTerminatorKind::MirCall { dest, func, args, success, unwind, intrinsic } then
      out_targets.push(success.id)
      match unwind
      when Option::Some(u) then out_targets.push(u.id)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    when MirTerminatorKind::MirAssert { cond, expected, msg, target, unwind } then
      out_targets.push(target.id)
      match unwind
      when Option::Some(u2) then out_targets.push(u2.id)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    when MirTerminatorKind::MirDeinit { place, deinit_fn, target, unwind } then
      out_targets.push(target.id)
      match unwind
      when Option::Some(u3) then out_targets.push(u3.id)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    when _ then ()
    end
    var ti = 0
    while ti < out_targets.len() do
      var tv = -1
      match block_of_id.get(out_targets[ti])
      when Option::Some(v2) then tv = v2
      when Option::None then ()
      end
      if tv >= 0 && tv != pi then
        var pred_rows: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
        match preds.get(tv)
        when Option::Some(rows) then pred_rows = rows.clone()
        when Option::None then ()
        end
        if !pred_rows.contains(&pi) then
          pred_rows.push(pi)
          preds.insert(tv, pred_rows)
        end
        var succ_rows: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
        match succs.get(pi)
        when Option::Some(srows) then succ_rows = srows.clone()
        when Option::None then ()
        end
        if !succ_rows.contains(&tv) then
          succ_rows.push(tv)
          succs.insert(pi, succ_rows)
        end
      end
      ti = ti + 1
    end
    pi = pi + 1
  end
  Option::Some(SliceFnCtx {
    name: name.clone(),
    f: f,
    block_of_id: block_of_id,
    preds: preds,
    succs: succs
  })
end

# The block Vec index of a block id (-1 when absent).
def slice_block_vec_index(ctx: SliceFnCtx, block_id: Int) -> Int
  match ctx.block_of_id.get(block_id)
  when Option::Some(v) then v
  when Option::None then -1
  end
end

# The emission-name -> function index map (the §11 scan's fn index).
def slice_fn_index(mir: MirProgram) -> Map[String, Int]
  var out: Map[String, Int] = Map::new()
  var i = 0
  while i < mir.functions.len() do
    let n = mir.functions[i].name.clone()
    if !out.contains_key(&n) then
      out.insert(n, i)
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  out
end

# The §11 type name index: MirTypeDef id -> registered type name.
def slice_type_index(mir: MirProgram) -> Map[Int, String]
  var out: Map[Int, String] = Map::new()
  for td in mir.types do
    out.insert(td.id.id, td.name.clone())
  end
  out
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Node reads and defs — the def-use atoms (the mir.tg optimizer
# vocabulary, self-contained)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# The local read by a MirOperand (None for constants — collect_operand_read
# shape).
def slice_operand_read(op: MirOperand) -> Option[Int]
  match op.kind
  when MirOperandKind::MirCopy(place) then Option::Some(place.local.id)
  when MirOperandKind::MirMovePlace(place) then Option::Some(place.local.id)
  when MirOperandKind::MirRead(place) then Option::Some(place.local.id)
  when MirOperandKind::MirConsume(place) then Option::Some(place.local.id)
  when _ then Option::None
  end
end

# The BARE root of a place-kind operand (mir.tg's mir_operand_bare_root):
# Some(local) for a place with EMPTY projections; None for projected
# places and constants.
def slice_operand_bare_root(op: MirOperand) -> Option[Int]
  match op.kind
  when MirOperandKind::MirCopy(p) then
    if p.projections.is_empty() then Option::Some(p.local.id) else Option::None end
  when MirOperandKind::MirMovePlace(p) then
    if p.projections.is_empty() then Option::Some(p.local.id) else Option::None end
  when MirOperandKind::MirRead(p) then
    if p.projections.is_empty() then Option::Some(p.local.id) else Option::None end
  when MirOperandKind::MirConsume(p) then
    if p.projections.is_empty() then Option::Some(p.local.id) else Option::None end
  when _ then Option::None
  end
end

# The rvalue reads (collect_rvalue_reads shape: every operand / place /
# phi-source local).
def slice_rvalue_reads(rv: MirRvalueKind, inout out: Vec[Int]) -> Unit
  match rv
  when MirRvalueKind::MirMove(op) then
    match slice_operand_read(&op)
    when Option::Some(l) then out.push(l)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirRef(place) then out.push(place.local.id)
  when MirRvalueKind::MirAggregate(_, ops) then
    for op in ops do
      match slice_operand_read(&op)
      when Option::Some(l2) then out.push(l2)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirBinOp(_, lhs, rhs) then
    match slice_operand_read(&lhs)
    when Option::Some(la) then out.push(la)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    match slice_operand_read(&rhs)
    when Option::Some(ra) then out.push(ra)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirUnOp(_, op) then
    match slice_operand_read(&op)
    when Option::Some(u) then out.push(u)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirDiscriminant(place) then out.push(place.local.id)
  when MirRvalueKind::MirLen(place) then out.push(place.local.id)
  when MirRvalueKind::MirCast(_, op, _) then
    match slice_operand_read(&op)
    when Option::Some(c) then out.push(c)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirRepeat(op, _) then
    match slice_operand_read(&op)
    when Option::Some(r) then out.push(r)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirPhi(entries) then
    for entry in entries do
      out.push(entry.1.id)
    end
  end
end

# Whether a call argument observes its operand's value — collect_call_arg_read's
# refinement: BARE Initialize args are writes, everything else reads.
def slice_call_arg_read(arg: MirCallArg) -> Option[Int]
  match arg.value
  when MirCallValue::Place(p) then
    match arg.effect
    when AccessEffect::Initialize then
      if p.projections.is_empty() then Option::None else Option::Some(p.local.id) end
    when _ then Option::Some(p.local.id)
    end
  when MirCallValue::Value(op) then
    match arg.effect
    when AccessEffect::Initialize then
      match slice_operand_bare_root(&op)
      when Option::Some(_) then Option::None
      when Option::None then slice_operand_read(&op)
      end
    when _ then slice_operand_read(&op)
    end
  end
end

# The reads of one MirStatement (its operands only — the DEST is a def).
def slice_stmt_reads(st: MirStatement) -> Vec[Int]
  var out: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
  match st.kind
  when MirStatementKind::MirAssign(_, rvalue) then
    slice_rvalue_reads(rvalue.kind, &mut out)
  when MirStatementKind::MirContractCheck(contract, operand) then
    match slice_operand_read(&contract.condition)
    when Option::Some(c) then out.push(c)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    match slice_operand_read(&operand)
    when Option::Some(o) then out.push(o)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirStatementKind::MirEffectRecord(_, operand) then
    match slice_operand_read(&operand)
    when Option::Some(e) then out.push(e)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirStatementKind::MirEffectPerform(_, _, _, payload_ptr, result_ptr) then
    match slice_operand_read(&payload_ptr)
    when Option::Some(p) then out.push(p)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    match slice_operand_read(&result_ptr)
    when Option::Some(r) then out.push(r)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirStatementKind::MirEffectFrameEnter(_, _, _, _, env_ptr) then
    match slice_operand_read(&env_ptr)
    when Option::Some(e2) then out.push(e2)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when _ then ()
  end
  out
end

# The terminator reads — collect_terminator_reads shape plus MirDeinit-reads-its-place
# and MirReturn-reads-local-0 ("_ret").
def slice_term_reads(term: MirTerminator) -> Vec[Int]
  var out: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
  match term.kind
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirSwitchInt { op, targets, default_target } then
    match slice_operand_read(&op)
    when Option::Some(s) then out.push(s)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirCall { dest, func, args, success, unwind, intrinsic } then
    match slice_operand_read(&func)
    when Option::Some(c) then out.push(c)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    for arg in args do
      match slice_call_arg_read(&arg)
      when Option::Some(a) then out.push(a)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    end
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirAssert { cond, expected, msg, target, unwind } then
    match slice_operand_read(&cond)
    when Option::Some(cc) then out.push(cc)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    match msg
    when AssertMessage::BoundsCheck(index_op, len_op) then
      match slice_operand_read(&index_op)
      when Option::Some(io) then out.push(io)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
      match slice_operand_read(&len_op)
      when Option::Some(lo) then out.push(lo)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    when _ then ()
    end
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirDeinit { place, deinit_fn, target, unwind } then
    # a destruction reads the value's current content — its final use.
    out.push(place.local.id)
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirReturn then
    # locals[0] is the function's return place ("_ret"): MirReturn leaves
    # it behind and therefore reads it.
    out.push(0)
  when _ then ()
  end
  out
end

# Node defs as (bare local, partial root), -1 = none: a bare write ENDS a def
# chain; a projected dest AFFECTS its root but does not end the chain.
def slice_stmt_defs(st: MirStatement) -> (Int, Int)
  match st.kind
  when MirStatementKind::MirAssign(place, _) then
    if place.projections.is_empty() then
      (place.local.id, -1)
    else
      (-1, place.local.id)
    end
  when _ then (-1, -1)
  end
end

def slice_term_defs(term: MirTerminator) -> (Int, Int)
  match term.kind
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirCall { dest, func, args, success, unwind, intrinsic } then
    if dest.projections.is_empty() then
      (dest.local.id, -1)
    else
      (-1, dest.local.id)
    end
  when _ then (-1, -1)
  end
end

# The callee emission name of a named MirCall (the MirFnItem constant's
# name); "" for value/indirect calls (no row identity — documented).
def slice_call_callee_name(term: MirTerminator) -> String
  match term.kind
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirCall { dest, func, args, success, unwind, intrinsic } then
    match func.kind
    when MirOperandKind::MirConstant(c) then
      match c.kind
      when MirConstantKind::MirFnItem(name) then return name.clone()
      when _ then return ""
      end
    when _ then return ""
    end
  when _ then ""
  end
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The backward engine — def chains of wanted locals
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Work items (block, from, local) resolve def chains backward: the first BARE
# def is included and its reads become new items; a PARTIAL def is included
# but the local STAYS wanted (the aggregate base is defined earlier); a scan
# ending at the block head propagates to the PREDECESSORS; a want reaching
# the ENTRY head resolves as a parameter anchor or drops silently. Dedupe
# texts + the item budget terminate cyclic pred graphs deterministically.

struct SliceBack
  ctx: SliceFnCtx
  # work items: (block Vec index, from node index inclusive, local id).
  work: Vec[(Int, Int, Int)] = Vec::new()
  # processed-item dedupe texts ("<block>@<from>#<local>").
  seen: Set[String] = Set::new()
  # included nodes: stmt key -> presentation span key ("" when dummy).
  included: Map[String, String] = Map::new()
  # external anchors ("param:<index>:<name>").
  external: Set[String] = Set::new()
  # items popped so far (the budget).
  items: Int = 0
end

def slice_back_item_text(v: Int, from: Int, local: Int) -> String
  v.to_string() + "@" + from.to_string() + "#" + local.to_string()
end

def slice_back_push(inout back: SliceBack, v: Int, from: Int, local: Int) -> Unit
  if v < 0 then return end
  let key = slice_back_item_text(v, from, local)
  if back.seen.contains(&key) then return end
  back.seen.insert(key)
  back.work.push((v, from, local))
  ()
end

def slice_back_include(inout back: SliceBack, v: Int, idx: Int, span: Span) -> Unit
  let block_id = back.ctx.f.blocks[v].id.id
  let block_len = back.ctx.f.blocks[v].statements.len()
  var node_key = ""
  if idx >= block_len then
    node_key = slice_term_key(&back.ctx.name, block_id)
  else
    node_key = slice_stmt_key(&back.ctx.name, block_id, idx)
  end
  if !back.included.contains_key(&node_key) then
    let span_key = slice_span_key(&node_key, span)
    back.included.insert(node_key, span_key)
  end
  ()
end

# Whether a local is a parameter of the ctx function (the def chain's
# caller-side boundary).
def slice_is_param(ctx: SliceFnCtx, local: Int) -> Bool
  for p in ctx.f.params do
    if p.id.id == local then
      return true
    end
  end
  false
end

def slice_back_external_param(inout back: SliceBack, local: Int) -> Unit
  if local >= 0 && local < back.ctx.f.locals.len() then
    let name = back.ctx.f.locals[local].name.clone()
    back.external.insert("param:" + local.to_string() + ":" + name)
  end
  ()
end

# Run the worklist to the budget (FIFO, deterministic).
def slice_back_run(inout back: SliceBack) -> Unit
  while back.work.len() > 0 && back.items < slice_max_items() do
    back.items = back.items + 1
    let item = back.work[0]
    back.work.remove(0)
    let v = item.0
    let from = item.1
    let wanted = item.2
    let block_len = back.ctx.f.blocks[v].statements.len()
    var found = false
    # the terminator is the first candidate when the scan starts at or
    # after the block end (a def in the terminator feeds the entry of a
    # SUCCESSOR block; it can never feed a use in this block).
    if from >= block_len then
      let term = back.ctx.f.blocks[v].terminator
      let term_defs = slice_term_defs(&term)
      let bare = term_defs.0
      let partial = term_defs.1
      if bare == wanted then
        let span = slice_span_copy(term.span)
        slice_back_include(&mut back, v, block_len, span)
        found = true
        let reads = slice_term_reads(&term)
        for r in reads do
          slice_back_push(&mut back, v, block_len - 1, r)
        end
      elsif partial == wanted then
        # a projected terminator write affects the value but does not end
        # the chain: include it, feed its operand reads, keep scanning.
        let span = slice_span_copy(term.span)
        slice_back_include(&mut back, v, block_len, span)
        let reads = slice_term_reads(&term)
        for r in reads do
          slice_back_push(&mut back, v, block_len - 1, r)
        end
      end
    end
    # then the statements, from the scan start down to the block head.
    var si = from
    if si > block_len - 1 then
      si = block_len - 1
    end
    while si >= 0 && !found do
      let st = back.ctx.f.blocks[v].statements[si]
      let st_defs = slice_stmt_defs(st)
      let bare = st_defs.0
      let partial = st_defs.1
      if bare == wanted then
        let span = slice_span_copy(st.span)
        slice_back_include(&mut back, v, si, span)
        found = true
        let reads = slice_stmt_reads(st)
        for r in reads do
          slice_back_push(&mut back, v, si - 1, r)
        end
      elsif partial == wanted then
        # a projected write affects the value but does not end the chain
        # (the aggregate base is defined earlier): include it, feed its
        # operand reads, keep scanning for the base def.
        let span = slice_span_copy(st.span)
        slice_back_include(&mut back, v, si, span)
        let reads = slice_stmt_reads(st)
        for r in reads do
          slice_back_push(&mut back, v, si - 1, r)
        end
      end
      si = si - 1
    end
    if !found then
      if slice_is_param(back.ctx.clone(), wanted) then
        slice_back_external_param(&mut back, wanted)
      else
        var pred_rows: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
        match back.ctx.preds.get(v)
        when Option::Some(rows) then pred_rows = rows.clone()
        when Option::None then ()
        end
        for p in pred_rows do
          let p_len = back.ctx.f.blocks[p].statements.len()
          slice_back_push(&mut back, p, p_len, wanted)
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ()
end

# Seed one anchored def-chain walk: the defs of `local` that feed its use
# at (block Vec index v, node index idx). The scan starts BELOW the use
# node (a def AT the use node — a call reading and writing the same
# local — feeds later uses, never this one).
def slice_backward_at(inout back: SliceBack, v: Int, idx: Int, local: Int) -> Unit
  slice_back_push(&mut back, v, idx - 1, local)
  slice_back_run(&mut back)
  ()
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The forward engine — transitive uses of a statement's defs
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Work items (block, from, local) follow a def forward: every node READING
# the local is included; a bare redefinition KILLS the chain (a partial
# redefinition passes through); an included node's own defs become new items
# (transitive uses). Chains surviving the terminator propagate to SUCCESSORS;
# a def escaping as a named call argument records the "call:<callee>:arg<n>"
# anchor. A MirDeinit consumes the local (the chain dies there).

struct SliceFwd
  ctx: SliceFnCtx
  # work items: (block Vec index, from node index inclusive, local id).
  work: Vec[(Int, Int, Int)] = Vec::new()
  seen: Set[String] = Set::new()
  included: Map[String, String] = Map::new()
  external: Set[String] = Set::new()
  items: Int = 0
end

def slice_fwd_push(inout fwd: SliceFwd, v: Int, from: Int, local: Int) -> Unit
  if v < 0 then return end
  let key = slice_back_item_text(v, from, local)
  if fwd.seen.contains(&key) then return end
  fwd.seen.insert(key)
  fwd.work.push((v, from, local))
  ()
end

def slice_fwd_include(inout fwd: SliceFwd, v: Int, idx: Int, span: Span) -> Unit
  let block_id = fwd.ctx.f.blocks[v].id.id
  let block_len = fwd.ctx.f.blocks[v].statements.len()
  var node_key = ""
  if idx >= block_len then
    node_key = slice_term_key(&fwd.ctx.name, block_id)
  else
    node_key = slice_stmt_key(&fwd.ctx.name, block_id, idx)
  end
  if !fwd.included.contains_key(&node_key) then
    let span_key = slice_span_key(&node_key, span)
    fwd.included.insert(node_key, span_key)
  end
  ()
end

# "call:<callee>:arg<n>" anchors for every arg of a named call reading the
# tracked local (the def's escape edges).
def slice_fwd_call_anchors(term: MirTerminator, local: Int) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  let callee = slice_call_callee_name(term)
  if callee.len() == 0 then return out end
  match term.kind
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirCall { dest, func, args, success, unwind, intrinsic } then
    var ai = 0
    while ai < args.len() do
      match slice_call_arg_read(&args[ai])
      when Option::Some(l) then
        if l == local then
          out.push("call:" + callee.clone() + ":arg" + ai.to_string())
        end
      when Option::None then ()
      end
      ai = ai + 1
    end
  when _ then ()
  end
  out
end

# Run the forward worklist to the budget (FIFO, deterministic).
def slice_fwd_run(inout fwd: SliceFwd) -> Unit
  while fwd.work.len() > 0 && fwd.items < slice_max_items() do
    fwd.items = fwd.items + 1
    let item = fwd.work[0]
    fwd.work.remove(0)
    let v = item.0
    let from = item.1
    let local = item.2
    let block_len = fwd.ctx.f.blocks[v].statements.len()
    var killed = false
    var si = from
    while si < block_len && !killed do
      let st = fwd.ctx.f.blocks[v].statements[si]
      let st_defs = slice_stmt_defs(st)
      let bare = st_defs.0
      let reads = slice_stmt_reads(st)
      var uses = false
      for r in reads do
        if r == local then
          uses = true
        end
      end
      if uses then
        let span = slice_span_copy(st.span)
        slice_fwd_include(&mut fwd, v, si, span)
        # the value flows through this node: its own def (when any) is a
        # transitive carrier of the sliced def.
        if bare >= 0 then
          slice_fwd_push(&mut fwd, v, si + 1, bare)
        end
      end
      if bare == local then
        # the sliced def is overwritten here — its life ends at this node
        # (a read at the same node was already counted above).
        killed = true
      end
      si = si + 1
    end
    if !killed && from <= block_len then
      # the block terminator is a candidate node of the chain.
      let term = fwd.ctx.f.blocks[v].terminator
      let term_defs = slice_term_defs(&term)
      let bare = term_defs.0
      let reads = slice_term_reads(&term)
      var uses = false
      for r in reads do
        if r == local then
          uses = true
        end
      end
      if uses then
        let span = slice_span_copy(term.span)
        slice_fwd_include(&mut fwd, v, block_len, span)
        # a def read as a named call argument escapes through the call
        # edge: anchor the callee row even when the call's dest overwrites
        # the tracked local.
        let anchors = slice_fwd_call_anchors(&term, local)
        for a in anchors do
          fwd.external.insert(a.clone())
        end
        if bare >= 0 then
          slice_fwd_push(&mut fwd, v, block_len + 1, bare)
        end
      end
      if bare == local then
        killed = true
      end
      match term.kind
      when MirTerminatorKind::MirDeinit { place, deinit_fn, target, unwind } then
        # a destruction consumes the value: the chain dies there (reads
        # after a drop are invalid verified MIR).
        if place.local.id == local then
          killed = true
        end
      when _ then ()
      end
    end
    if !killed then
      # the chain survived the block: the value flows to the successors.
      var succ_rows: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
      match fwd.ctx.succs.get(v)
      when Option::Some(rows) then succ_rows = rows.clone()
      when Option::None then ()
      end
      for s in succ_rows do
        slice_fwd_push(&mut fwd, s, 0, local)
      end
    end
  end
  ()
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Result assembly — sorted stable ids + presentation span keys
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

def slice_result_build(ctx: SliceFnCtx, included: Map[String, String], external: Set[String]) -> SliceResult
  var keys: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  var entries: Vec[(String, String)] = included.entries()
  for entry in entries do
    keys.push(entry.0.clone())
  end
  keys.sort_by(|a, b| a < b)
  var span_rows: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for k in keys do
    match included.get(k.clone())
    when Option::Some(span_key) then
      if span_key.len() > 0 then
        span_rows.push(span_key.clone())
      end
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  end
  var exts: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for e in external do
    exts.push(e.clone())
  end
  exts.sort_by(|a, b| a < b)
  SliceResult {
    function_key: ctx.name.clone(),
    statements: keys,
    external: exts,
    span_keys: span_rows
  }
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# slice_value — the backward def chain of one value
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Seeds one anchored walk per USE SITE of the value (a node reading the
# local; a MirReturn reads the "_ret" local 0). A value with NO use sites
# yields the empty slice (nothing later observes it — documented).

pub def slice_value(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String, value_id: Int) -> SliceResult
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    if value_id < 0 || value_id >= ctx.f.locals.len() then
      return slice_result_empty()
    end
    var back = SliceBack { ctx: ctx, work: Vec::new(), seen: Set::new(), included: Map::new(), external: Set::new(), items: 0 }
    # seed one anchored def-chain walk per USE SITE of the value (a node
    # reading the local; a MirReturn reads the "_ret" local 0). A value
    # with no use sites yields the empty slice (documented).
    var bi = 0
    while bi < back.ctx.f.blocks.len() do
      let block_len = back.ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements.len()
      var si = 0
      while si < block_len do
        let st = back.ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements[si]
        let reads = slice_stmt_reads(st)
        for r in reads do
          if r == value_id then
            slice_backward_at(&mut back, bi, si, value_id)
          end
        end
        si = si + 1
      end
      let term = back.ctx.f.blocks[bi].terminator
      let treads = slice_term_reads(&term)
      for tr in treads do
        if tr == value_id then
          slice_backward_at(&mut back, bi, block_len, value_id)
        end
      end
      bi = bi + 1
    end
    slice_result_build(&back.ctx, &back.included, &back.external)
  when Option::None then slice_result_empty()
  end
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# slice_statement — the forward use slice of one statement's defs
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

pub def slice_statement(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String, stmt_key: String) -> SliceResult
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    match slice_key_parts(&fn_key, &stmt_key)
    when Option::Some(parts) then
      let block_id = parts.0
      let node_idx = parts.1
      let is_term = parts.2
      let v = slice_block_vec_index(&ctx, block_id)
      if v < 0 || v >= ctx.f.blocks.len() then
        return slice_result_empty()
      end
      let block_len = ctx.f.blocks[v].statements.len()
      var defs = (-1, -1)
      if is_term then
        defs = slice_term_defs(&ctx.f.blocks[v].terminator)
      elsif node_idx >= 0 && node_idx < block_len then
        let st = ctx.f.blocks[v].statements[node_idx]
        defs = slice_stmt_defs(st)
      end
      if defs.0 < 0 && defs.1 < 0 then
        # a node with no defs defines nothing for later nodes to use
        # (asserts, checks, switches...): the use slice is empty
        # (documented).
        return slice_result_empty()
      end
      var fwd = SliceFwd { ctx: ctx, work: Vec::new(), seen: Set::new(), included: Map::new(), external: Set::new(), items: 0 }
      var seed = defs.0
      if seed < 0 then
        seed = defs.1
      end
      var from = node_idx + 1
      if is_term then
        from = block_len + 1
      end
      slice_fwd_push(&mut fwd, v, from, seed)
      slice_fwd_run(&mut fwd)
      slice_result_build(&fwd.ctx, &fwd.included, &fwd.external)
    when Option::None then slice_result_empty()
    end
  when Option::None then slice_result_empty()
  end
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# slice_failure — the statements contributing to one diagnostic
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Trace + anchored condition slices of the mapped failing node (see the SPAN
# MAP section of the module doc).

# Whether a span textually contains the diagnostic start offset (empty
# files compare equal; a dummy span contains nothing).
def slice_span_contains(span: Span, d: Span) -> Bool
  if span.start == 0 && span.end_pos == 0 && span.file.len() == 0 then
    return false
  end
  if d.file.len() > 0 && span.file.len() > 0 && d.file != span.file then
    return false
  end
  span.start <= d.start && d.start <= span.end_pos
end

# The strict better-than relation over mapping tiers (see above); the
# walk replaces only on strictly-better, so ties keep the EARLIER node.
def slice_span_better(a: Span, b: Span, d: Span) -> Bool
  var a_contain = slice_span_contains(&a, &d)
  var b_contain = slice_span_contains(&b, &d)
  if a_contain != b_contain then
    return a_contain
  end
  var a_overlap = (a.start <= d.end_pos) && (d.start <= a.end_pos)
  var b_overlap = (b.start <= d.end_pos) && (d.start <= b.end_pos)
  if a_overlap != b_overlap then
    return a_overlap
  end
  var a_gap = a.start - d.start
  if a_gap < 0 then a_gap = -a_gap end
  var b_gap = b.start - d.start
  if b_gap < 0 then b_gap = -b_gap end
  if a_gap != b_gap then
    return a_gap < b_gap
  end
  var a_egap = a.end_pos - d.end_pos
  if a_egap < 0 then a_egap = -a_egap end
  var b_egap = b.end_pos - d.end_pos
  if b_egap < 0 then b_egap = -b_egap end
  a_egap < b_egap
end

# The best-mapped (ctx, block Vec index, node index); None when nothing maps.
def slice_failure_map(mir: MirProgram, diag: Diagnostic) -> Option[(SliceFnCtx, Int, Int)]
  match diag.span.clone()
  when Option::Some(dspan) then
    var best_ctx: Option[SliceFnCtx] = Option::None
    var best_v = -1
    var best_idx = -1
    var best_span = Span { file: "", start: 0, end_pos: 0 }
    var best_set = false
    for f in mir.functions do
      match slice_fn_find(mir, f.name.clone())
      when Option::Some(ctx) then
        var bi = 0
        while bi < ctx.f.blocks.len() do
          let block_len = ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements.len()
          var si = 0
          while si < block_len do
            let st = ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements[si]
            let sp = slice_span_copy(st.span)
            if !best_set || slice_span_better(&sp, &best_span, &dspan) then
              best_set = true
              best_span = sp
              best_ctx = Option::Some(ctx.clone())
              best_v = bi
              best_idx = si
            end
            si = si + 1
          end
          let term = ctx.f.blocks[bi].terminator
          let tsp = slice_span_copy(term.span)
          if !best_set || slice_span_better(&tsp, &best_span, &dspan) then
            best_set = true
            best_span = tsp
            best_ctx = Option::Some(ctx.clone())
            best_v = bi
            best_idx = block_len
          end
          bi = bi + 1
        end
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    end
    match best_ctx
    when Option::Some(bc) then Option::Some((bc, best_v, best_idx))
    when Option::None then Option::None
    end
  when Option::None then Option::None
  end
end

# The node-anchored FAILURE slice: the failing node's read operands' anchored
# def chains UNION the failure trace (the enclosing block's statements from
# its head through the node — the failing terminator included). Shared by
# slice_failure (span-mapped anchors through slice_failure_map) and the typed
# mir_slice Failure kind (direct node-key anchors).
def slice_failure_node_slice(ctx: SliceFnCtx, v: Int, idx: Int) -> SliceResult
  let block_len = ctx.f.blocks[v].statements.len()
  var back = SliceBack { ctx: ctx.clone(), work: Vec::new(), seen: Set::new(), included: Map::new(), external: Set::new(), items: 0 }
  # the failing node's read operands (the failing condition and its
  # bounds, the switch scrutinee, the call's arguments...): the anchored
  # def chains of each.
  var reads: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
  if idx >= block_len then
    let term = ctx.f.blocks[v].terminator
    reads = slice_term_reads(&term)
  else
    let st = ctx.f.blocks[v].statements[idx]
    reads = slice_stmt_reads(st)
  end
  for r in reads do
    slice_backward_at(&mut back, v, idx, r)
  end
  # the failure trace: the enclosing block's statements from its head
  # through the failing node (the failing terminator included).
  var ti = 0
  while ti <= idx && ti <= block_len do
    var node_key = ""
    var nspan = Span { file: "", start: 0, end_pos: 0 }
    if ti >= block_len then
      node_key = slice_term_key(&ctx.name, ctx.f.blocks[v].id.id)
      nspan = slice_span_copy(ctx.f.blocks[v].terminator.span)
    else
      node_key = slice_stmt_key(&ctx.name, ctx.f.blocks[v].id.id, ti)
      nspan = slice_span_copy(ctx.f.blocks[v].statements[ti].span)
    end
    if !back.included.contains_key(&node_key) then
      let span_key = slice_span_key(&node_key, nspan)
      back.included.insert(node_key, span_key)
    end
    ti = ti + 1
  end
  slice_result_build(&ctx, &back.included, &back.external)
end

pub def slice_failure(mir: MirProgram, diag: Diagnostic) -> SliceResult
  match slice_failure_map(mir, diag)
  when Option::Some(triple) then slice_failure_node_slice(triple.0, triple.1, triple.2)
  when Option::None then slice_result_empty()
  end
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# slice_effect — the statements contributing one effect class
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# One row per function whose DIRECT §11 summary has the class: the class's
# direct sites (per the §11 evidence — classify_call/_deinit reuse, the
# string-concat MirBinOp::Add, the fail-closed perform) + each site's
# anchored def chains of the values it reads (the module doc's model).

# Per-statement class evidence (3 slots: Alloc/Block/Io per
# effect_class_slot_index), mirroring mir_effect_scan_function's two arms.
def slice_stmt_effect_evidence(f: MirFunction, st: MirStatement) -> Vec[String]
  var ev: Vec[String] = Vec::from(["".to_string(), "".to_string(), "".to_string()])
  match st.kind
  when MirStatementKind::MirAssign(dest, rvalue) then
    match rvalue.kind
    when MirRvalueKind::MirBinOp(MirBinOp::Add, lhs, rhs) then
      let dest_ty = mir_effect_place_type(&f, &dest)
      let dest_str = mir_effect_type_is_string_like(&dest_ty)
      let lhs_str = mir_effect_operand_is_string(&f, &lhs)
      let rhs_str = mir_effect_operand_is_string(&f, &rhs)
      if dest_str || lhs_str || rhs_str then
        ev[0] = "the `+` String concatenation (the _tg_str_concat owned heap String wrap)"
      end
    when _ then ()
    end
  when MirStatementKind::MirEffectPerform(_, _, _, _, _) then
    ev[0] = "an algebraic-effects perform whose handler's allocation behavior cannot be proven"
    ev[1] = "an algebraic-effects perform whose handler's blocking behavior cannot be proven"
    ev[2] = "an algebraic-effects perform whose handler's I/O behavior cannot be proven"
  when _ then ()
  end
  ev
end

# Per-terminator class evidence (the §11 classifier's direct records;
# assert/abort sites are panic-class only).
def slice_term_effect_evidence(mir: MirProgram, f: MirFunction, term: MirTerminator, type_index: Map[Int, String], fn_index: Map[String, Int]) -> Vec[String]
  var ev: Vec[String] = Vec::from(["".to_string(), "".to_string(), "".to_string()])
  match term.kind
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirCall { dest, func, args, success, unwind, intrinsic } then
    let cc = mir_effect_classify_call(mir, &f, &type_index, &fn_index, &func, &args, intrinsic)
    var i = 0
    while i < 3 && i < cc.evidence.len() do
      ev[i] = cc.evidence[i].clone()
      i = i + 1
    end
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirDeinit { place, deinit_fn, target, unwind } then
    let cd = mir_effect_classify_deinit(mir, &fn_index, &deinit_fn)
    var i2 = 0
    while i2 < 3 && i2 < cd.evidence.len() do
      ev[i2] = cd.evidence[i2].clone()
      i2 = i2 + 1
    end
  when _ then ()
  end
  ev
end

pub def slice_effect(mir: MirProgram, class: EffectClass) -> Vec[SliceResult]
  let type_index = slice_type_index(&mir)
  let fn_index = slice_fn_index(&mir)
  var state = MirEffectState {}
  for f in mir.functions do
    mir_effect_scan_function(&mir, &mut state, &type_index, &fn_index, &f)
  end
  var slot = effect_class_slot_index(class)
  var rows_by_name: Map[String, SliceResult] = Map::new()
  var seen_fns: Set[String] = Set::new()
  for f in mir.functions do
    var summary = EffectSummary {}
    match state.direct.get(f.name.clone())
    when Option::Some(s) then summary = s.clone()
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    if effect_summary_has_class(&summary, &class) then
      if !seen_fns.contains(&f.name) then
        seen_fns.insert(f.name.clone())
        match slice_fn_find(&mir, f.name.clone())
        when Option::Some(ctx) then
          var back = SliceBack { ctx: ctx.clone(), work: Vec::new(), seen: Set::new(), included: Map::new(), external: Set::new(), items: 0 }
          var bi = 0
          while bi < ctx.f.blocks.len() do
            let block_id = ctx.f.blocks[bi].id.id
            let block_len = ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements.len()
            var si = 0
            while si < block_len do
              let st = ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements[si]
              let ev = slice_stmt_effect_evidence(&f, st)
              if slot < ev.len() && ev[slot].len() > 0 then
                let node_key = slice_stmt_key(&ctx.name, block_id, si)
                if !back.included.contains_key(&node_key) then
                  let nspan = slice_span_copy(st.span)
                  let span_key = slice_span_key(&node_key, nspan)
                  back.included.insert(node_key, span_key)
                end
                let reads = slice_stmt_reads(st)
                for r in reads do
                  slice_backward_at(&mut back, bi, si, r)
                end
              end
              si = si + 1
            end
            let term = ctx.f.blocks[bi].terminator
            let tev = slice_term_effect_evidence(&mir, &f, &term, &type_index, &fn_index)
            if slot < tev.len() && tev[slot].len() > 0 then
              let node_key = slice_term_key(&ctx.name, block_id)
              if !back.included.contains_key(&node_key) then
                let nspan = slice_span_copy(term.span)
                let span_key = slice_span_key(&node_key, nspan)
                back.included.insert(node_key, span_key)
              end
              let treads = slice_term_reads(&term)
              for tr in treads do
                slice_backward_at(&mut back, bi, block_len, tr)
              end
            end
            bi = bi + 1
          end
          let row = slice_result_build(&ctx, &back.included, &back.external)
          rows_by_name.insert(f.name.clone(), row)
        when Option::None then ()
        end
      end
    end
  end
  # rows sorted by function key (deterministic order).
  var names: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  var entries: Vec[(String, SliceResult)] = rows_by_name.entries()
  for entry in entries do
    names.push(entry.0.clone())
  end
  names.sort_by(|a, b| a < b)
  var sorted: Vec[SliceResult] = Vec::new()
  for n in names do
    match rows_by_name.get(n.clone())
    when Option::Some(r2) then sorted.push(r2.clone())
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  end
  sorted
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# slice_digest — the content-addressed digest of slice results
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The digest preimage is the SORTED canonical JSONL row set of the
# results (function / statement / external rows — the semantic_index.tg
# line style). span_keys NEVER serialize (spans are presentation, never
# identity).

def slice_digest_lines(results: Vec[SliceResult]) -> Vec[String]
  var lines: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  lines.push("{\"s\":\"header\",\"format\":\"tg-semantic-slice/v1\"}")
  for r in results do
    let fkey = r.function_key.clone()
    if fkey.len() > 0 then
      lines.push("{\"s\":\"slice\",\"f\":\"" + semantic_json_escape(&fkey) + "\"}")
      for k in r.statements do
        lines.push("{\"s\":\"stmt\",\"f\":\"" + semantic_json_escape(&fkey) + "\",\"k\":\"" + semantic_json_escape(&k) + "\"}")
      end
      for e in r.external do
        lines.push("{\"s\":\"ext\",\"f\":\"" + semantic_json_escape(&fkey) + "\",\"k\":\"" + semantic_json_escape(&e) + "\"}")
      end
    end
  end
  lines.sort_by(|a, b| a < b)
  lines
end

pub def slice_digest(results: Vec[SliceResult]) -> StableDigest
  var text = ""
  let lines = slice_digest_lines(results)
  for l in lines do
    text = text + l + "\n"
  end
  stable_digest_of(&text)
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# THE TYPED §33 SLICE ENTRY (audit item 22) — mir_slice
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# mir_slice is the ONE typed slicing entry over an optional verified
# MirProgram: a MirSliceRequest (function_key + kind + anchor) in, a typed
# Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError] out. The four slices above stay the
# engines; each MirSliceKind routes onto them (plus the module-local
# ControlDependence / Ownership walks below):
#
#   BackwardDataflow   → slice_value-style backward def chains.
#   ForwardDataflow    → slice_statement-style forward use chains.
#   ControlDependence  → the bounded CFG-predecessor walk below.
#   Ownership          → the place-family walk below.
#   Effects            → slice_effect's §11 classifier row of the fn.
#   Failure            → the node-anchored slice_failure machinery.
#   ReturnValue        → the backward slice of the "_ret" local 0.
#
# REQUEST ANCHOR GRAMMAR (per kind):
#   node anchors    — the §33 statement/terminator key texts
#                     "<fn emission name>#B<block id>#S<stmt index>" and
#                     "<fn emission name>#B<block id>#T" (BackwardDataflow,
#                     ForwardDataflow, ControlDependence, Failure). The
#                     key's function prefix must equal the request's
#                     function_key (a foreign-prefixed key never resolves
#                     inside this function: AnchorNotFound).
#   local anchors   — the §27 local key text of ONE slot: the declared
#                     name (name-first over ALL slots, first-wins) or the
#                     "l<id>" locator of an unnamed slot; out-of-range ids
#                     never resolve (BackwardDataflow, ForwardDataflow):
#                     the slice of the LOCAL's value.
#   place anchors   — the §7 place key text (local root + projection
#                     segments: ".field"/".variant" names from the MIR
#                     type table, ".digits" tuple indexes, "[name]"/"[n]"
#                     element indexes, "*" derefs) whose root resolves to
#                     a local (Ownership). A root-only anchor matches the
#                     WHOLE place family of the local; a projected anchor
#                     matches exactly the anchored place and its textual
#                     descendants.
#   class words     — "alloc" / "block" / "io", plus the claim spellings
#                     "no_alloc" / "no_block" / "no_io" and the message
#                     words "allocation" / "blocking" / "I/O" (Effects).
#   ReturnValue     — the anchor text is ignored (pass "").
#
# ERROR MAPPING: Option::None → MirProgramUnavailable; a function_key
# naming no emission name → FunctionNotFound; an anchor that is not a key
# of its kind or whose key does not resolve (a missing block/statement, an
# unresolvable local/place root, an unknown class word) → AnchorNotFound.
# MirSliceError::UnsupportedKind is the RESERVED variant of the typed
# surface: every kind routes today, so the error never leaves the module
# (documented).
#
# The MirSlice payload carries the sorted statement key texts + sorted
# external anchors; span_keys never cross this boundary (spans are
# presentation-only per the module doc). Empty Ok slices are documented
# per kind: a node-anchored BackwardDataflow whose node reads nothing, a
# ForwardDataflow node whose defs nothing reads, an Effects request whose
# function has no DIRECT class row (a class reaching it only through
# in-program callees lives in the callee rows), a value with no use sites
# (slice_value's rule) and the CFG walks with nothing to report.

enum MirSliceKind
  BackwardDataflow
  ForwardDataflow
  ControlDependence
  Ownership
  Effects
  Failure
  ReturnValue
end

# ONE typed slice request. Anchor texts follow the per-kind grammar above.
struct MirSliceRequest
  function_key: String
  kind: MirSliceKind
  anchor: String
end

# The typed error of a slice request. UnsupportedKind is reserved (never
# produced: every MirSliceKind routes — documented above).
enum MirSliceError
  FunctionNotFound
  AnchorNotFound
  MirProgramUnavailable
  UnsupportedKind
end

# ONE typed slice result: the sorted stable statement key texts, the
# sorted external anchors and the kind that produced the row. span_keys do
# not ride this record (presentation-only, never identity).
struct MirSlice
  function_key: String
  statements: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  externals: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  kind: MirSliceKind
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Anchor parsers (the typed entry's key texts)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# A node-key anchor resolved inside a function ctx: (block Vec index, node
# index; the terminator's node index IS the block's statement count).
# Option::None when the key does not parse or names a missing node.
def slice_node_anchor_at(ctx: SliceFnCtx, anchor: String) -> Option[(Int, Int)]
  match slice_key_parts(&ctx.name, &anchor)
  when Option::Some(parts) then
    let block_id = parts.0
    let node_idx = parts.1
    let is_term = parts.2
    let v = slice_block_vec_index(&ctx, block_id)
    if v < 0 || v >= ctx.f.blocks.len() then
      return Option::None
    end
    let block_len = ctx.f.blocks[v].statements.len()
    if is_term then
      return Option::Some((v, block_len))
    end
    if node_idx >= 0 && node_idx < block_len then
      return Option::Some((v, node_idx))
    end
    Option::None
  when Option::None then Option::None
  end
end

# The canonical local key text of one slot (snapshot_local_name's grammar:
# the declared name when the slot has one, else the "l<id>" locator).
def slice_local_canonical_text(f: MirFunction, local: Int) -> String
  if local >= 0 && local < f.locals.len() then
    let name = f.locals[local].name.clone()
    if name.len() > 0 then
      return name
    end
  end
  "l" + local.to_string()
end

# A local/key anchor resolved inside a function ctx: the declared-name
# match first (over ALL slots, first-wins — a local literally named "l7"
# wins over the locator), then the "l<id>" locator of a slot in range.
# Option::None when neither resolves.
def slice_local_anchor_at(ctx: SliceFnCtx, anchor: String) -> Option[Int]
  var i = 0
  while i < ctx.f.locals.len() do
    if ctx.f.locals[i].name == anchor then
      return Option::Some(ctx.f.locals[i].id.id)
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  if anchor.len() > 1 && anchor.slice(0, 1) == "l" then
    let digits = anchor.slice(1, anchor.len())
    if digits.len() <= 9 && slice_is_digits(&digits) then
      let id = slice_text_to_int(&digits)
      if id >= 0 && id < ctx.f.locals.len() then
        return Option::Some(id)
      end
    end
  end
  Option::None
end

# The canonical spellings of an effect CLASS word (the claims' names, the
# class message words and the class names themselves).
def slice_effect_class_of_anchor(anchor: String) -> Option[EffectClass]
  if anchor == "alloc" || anchor == "no_alloc" || anchor == "allocation" then
    return Option::Some(EffectClass::Alloc)
  end
  if anchor == "block" || anchor == "no_block" || anchor == "blocking" then
    return Option::Some(EffectClass::Block)
  end
  if anchor == "io" || anchor == "no_io" || anchor == "I/O" then
    return Option::Some(EffectClass::Io)
  end
  Option::None
end

# Whether one rendered place text is AT or BELOW another (the anchored
# place itself or a projection descendant — boundary-aware, so "x.f" never
# matches "x.f2").
def slice_place_text_touches(anchor_text: String, place_text: String) -> Bool
  if place_text == anchor_text then
    return true
  end
  if place_text.len() > anchor_text.len() then
    if place_text.slice(0, anchor_text.len()) == anchor_text then
      let nxt = place_text.slice(anchor_text.len(), anchor_text.len() + 1)
      if nxt == "." || nxt == "[" || nxt == "*" then
        return true
      end
    end
  end
  false
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Place collectors — the operand/place keys of one node (the Ownership
# walk's atoms; place-payloaded mirrors of the reads collectors)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# The place of a place-kind operand (None for constants).
def slice_operand_place(op: MirOperand) -> Option[Place]
  match op.kind
  when MirOperandKind::MirCopy(p) then Option::Some(p)
  when MirOperandKind::MirMovePlace(p) then Option::Some(p)
  when MirOperandKind::MirRead(p) then Option::Some(p)
  when MirOperandKind::MirConsume(p) then Option::Some(p)
  when _ then Option::None
  end
end

# The rvalue's place sources (the slice_rvalue_reads mirror with the full
# places; MirPhi sources are VALUES — no places).
def slice_rvalue_places(rv: MirRvalueKind, inout out: Vec[Place]) -> Unit
  match rv
  when MirRvalueKind::MirMove(op) then
    match slice_operand_place(&op)
    when Option::Some(p) then out.push(p)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirRef(place) then out.push(place)
  when MirRvalueKind::MirAggregate(_, ops) then
    for op in ops do
      match slice_operand_place(&op)
      when Option::Some(p2) then out.push(p2)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirBinOp(_, lhs, rhs) then
    match slice_operand_place(&lhs)
    when Option::Some(la) then out.push(la)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    match slice_operand_place(&rhs)
    when Option::Some(ra) then out.push(ra)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirUnOp(_, op) then
    match slice_operand_place(&op)
    when Option::Some(u) then out.push(u)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirDiscriminant(place) then out.push(place)
  when MirRvalueKind::MirLen(place) then out.push(place)
  when MirRvalueKind::MirCast(_, op, _) then
    match slice_operand_place(&op)
    when Option::Some(c) then out.push(c)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirRvalueKind::MirRepeat(op, _) then
    match slice_operand_place(&op)
    when Option::Some(r) then out.push(r)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when _ then ()
  end
end

# The place of a call argument (Place-valued args and place-kind operand
# args; BARE write-args still touch their place — the ownership view keeps
# the site even when the dataflow read rule drops it).
def slice_call_arg_place(arg: MirCallArg) -> Option[Place]
  match arg.value
  when MirCallValue::Place(p) then Option::Some(p)
  when MirCallValue::Value(op) then slice_operand_place(&op)
  end
end

# The places one statement touches: the assignment DEST plus the rvalue's
# place sources (contract checks, effect records/performs and effect frame
# enters contribute their operand places).
def slice_stmt_places(st: MirStatement) -> Vec[Place]
  var out: Vec[Place] = Vec::new()
  match st.kind
  when MirStatementKind::MirAssign(dest, rvalue) then
    out.push(dest)
    slice_rvalue_places(rvalue.kind, &mut out)
  when MirStatementKind::MirContractCheck(contract, operand) then
    match slice_operand_place(&contract.condition)
    when Option::Some(c) then out.push(c)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    match slice_operand_place(&operand)
    when Option::Some(o) then out.push(o)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirStatementKind::MirEffectRecord(_, operand) then
    match slice_operand_place(&operand)
    when Option::Some(e) then out.push(e)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirStatementKind::MirEffectPerform(_, _, _, payload_ptr, result_ptr) then
    match slice_operand_place(&payload_ptr)
    when Option::Some(p) then out.push(p)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    match slice_operand_place(&result_ptr)
    when Option::Some(r) then out.push(r)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirStatementKind::MirEffectFrameEnter(_, _, _, _, env_ptr) then
    match slice_operand_place(&env_ptr)
    when Option::Some(e2) then out.push(e2)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when _ then ()
  end
  out
end

# The places one terminator touches: the switch scrutinee, the call's
# dest/func/arguments, the assert's condition (+ bounds operands), the
# deinit's place (a destruction IS a place touch).
def slice_term_places(term: MirTerminator) -> Vec[Place]
  var out: Vec[Place] = Vec::new()
  match term.kind
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirSwitchInt { op, targets: _, default_target: _ } then
    match slice_operand_place(&op)
    when Option::Some(s) then out.push(s)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirCall { dest, func, args, success: _, unwind: _, intrinsic: _ } then
    out.push(dest)
    match slice_operand_place(&func)
    when Option::Some(c) then out.push(c)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    for arg in args do
      match slice_call_arg_place(&arg)
      when Option::Some(a) then out.push(a)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    end
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirAssert { cond, expected: _, msg, target: _, unwind: _ } then
    match slice_operand_place(&cond)
    when Option::Some(cc) then out.push(cc)
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    match msg
    when AssertMessage::BoundsCheck(index_op, len_op) then
      match slice_operand_place(&index_op)
      when Option::Some(io) then out.push(io)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
      match slice_operand_place(&len_op)
      when Option::Some(lo) then out.push(lo)
      when Option::None then ()
      end
    when _ then ()
    end
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirDeinit { place, deinit_fn: _, target: _, unwind: _ } then
    out.push(place)
  when _ then ()
  end
  out
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Place-text rendering — the §7 canonical place key over the MIR type
# table (declaration names; a type the program table does not carry falls
# back to the deterministic "f<index>" / "v<index>" render — documented;
# the fallback never appears for verified programs whose types table is
# complete).
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# The struct FIELD name of an owner TypeId (the deterministic "f<index>"
# fallback when the owner is not a Struct of the program table).
def slice_field_name_text(mir: MirProgram, owner_id: Int, index: Int) -> String
  for td in mir.types do
    if td.id.id == owner_id then
      match td.kind
      when MirTypeDefKind::Struct(fields) then
        if index >= 0 && index < fields.len() then
          return fields[index].name.clone()
        end
      when _ then ()
      end
      return "f" + index.to_string()
    end
  end
  "f" + index.to_string()
end

# The enum VARIANT name of an owner TypeId (the deterministic "v<index>"
# fallback, see slice_field_name_text).
def slice_variant_name_text(mir: MirProgram, owner_id: Int, index: UInt) -> String
  let vi = index as Int
  for td in mir.types do
    if td.id.id == owner_id then
      match td.kind
      when MirTypeDefKind::Enum(variants) then
        if vi >= 0 && vi < variants.len() then
          return variants[vi].name.clone()
        end
      when _ then ()
      end
      return "v" + vi.to_string()
    end
  end
  "v" + vi.to_string()
end

# The canonical place key text of one place (the module doc's §7 grammar:
# canonical root local text + ".field"/".variant" name segments from the
# MIR type table, ".digits" tuple indexes, "[name]"/"[digits]" element
# indexes, "*" derefs).
def slice_render_place(mir: MirProgram, f: MirFunction, p: Place) -> String
  var text = slice_local_canonical_text(&f, p.local.id)
  for proj in p.projections do
    match proj
    when Projection::ProjDeref then text = text + "*"
    when Projection::Field(fid) then
      text = text + "." + slice_field_name_text(&mir, fid.owner.id, fid.index)
    when Projection::Variant(vid) then
      text = text + "." + slice_variant_name_text(&mir, vid.owner.id, vid.index)
    when Projection::TupleIndex(idx) then text = text + "." + idx.to_string()
    when Projection::ProjIndex(local_id) then
      text = text + "[" + slice_local_canonical_text(&f, local_id.id) + "]"
    when Projection::ProjConstantIndex(idx2) then text = text + "[" + idx2.to_string() + "]"
    end
  end
  text
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The Ownership walk — nodes whose operand/place keys touch the anchor
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# A root-only anchor (tail == "") matches the WHOLE place family rooted at
# the local (every node whose read/write/dest place has that root — the
# conservative family). A projected anchor (tail != "") matches the nodes
# whose rendered place key sits AT or BELOW the anchor's canonical text
# (slice_place_text_touches). One deterministic single pass over the
# function's nodes — no worklist, bounded by the function's size.

# Whether any collected place touches (root, tail) — see the walk doc.
def slice_places_touch(mir: MirProgram, f: MirFunction, places: Vec[Place], root: Int, tail: String) -> Bool
  if tail.len() == 0 then
    for p in places do
      if p.local.id == root then
        return true
      end
    end
    return false
  end
  let canonical = slice_local_canonical_text(&f, root) + tail
  for p in places do
    if p.local.id == root then
      let pkey = slice_render_place(&mir, &f, &p)
      if slice_place_text_touches(&canonical, &pkey) then
        return true
      end
    end
  end
  false
end

def slice_ownership_walk(mir: MirProgram, ctx: SliceFnCtx, root: Int, tail: String) -> SliceResult
  var included: Map[String, String] = Map::new()
  var bi = 0
  while bi < ctx.f.blocks.len() do
    let block_id = ctx.f.blocks[bi].id.id
    let block_len = ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements.len()
    var si = 0
    while si < block_len do
      let st = ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements[si]
      if slice_places_touch(&mir, &ctx.f, slice_stmt_places(st), root, &tail) then
        let node_key = slice_stmt_key(&ctx.name, block_id, si)
        if !included.contains_key(&node_key) then
          let nspan = slice_span_copy(st.span)
          included.insert(node_key, slice_span_key(&node_key, nspan))
        end
      end
      si = si + 1
    end
    if slice_places_touch(&mir, &ctx.f, slice_term_places(&ctx.f.blocks[bi].terminator), root, &tail) then
      let node_key = slice_term_key(&ctx.name, block_id)
      if !included.contains_key(&node_key) then
        let nspan = slice_span_copy(ctx.f.blocks[bi].terminator.span)
        included.insert(node_key, slice_span_key(&node_key, nspan))
      end
    end
    bi = bi + 1
  end
  let empty_ext: Set[String] = Set::new()
  slice_result_build(&ctx, &included, &empty_ext)
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The ControlDependence walk — conditional terminators deciding the anchor
# block's reachability
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# A bounded FIFO walk over the module's predecessor map (slice_fn_find
# builds it from the terminator targets; abort/unreachable/self edges are
# not modeled — documented above): every predecessor chain of the anchor
# block is visited once (deduped, capped at slice_max_items() popped
# blocks), and the CONDITIONAL terminators along the way — the branch
# sites that decide whether control reaches the anchor — are the slice's
# statements. Conditional = a switch/assert (the assert's condition
# decides target vs. abort) or a call/deinit WITH an unwind edge (the
# success-vs-unwind split); goto/return/abort/unreachable and
# unwind-free calls decide nothing in the modeled CFG. Pure CFG slice: the
# conditions' own def chains stay the dataflow kinds' business
# (documented); no external anchors.

# Whether a terminator is a conditional decision site (see the walk doc).
def slice_term_is_conditional(term: MirTerminator) -> Bool
  match term.kind
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirGoto(_) then false
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirReturn then false
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirUnreachable then false
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirSwitchInt { op: _, targets: _, default_target: _ } then true
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirCall { dest: _, func: _, args: _, success: _, unwind, intrinsic: _ } then
    match unwind
    when Option::Some(_) then true
    when Option::None then false
    end
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirAssert { cond: _, expected: _, msg: _, target: _, unwind: _ } then true
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirAbort then false
  when MirTerminatorKind::MirDeinit { place: _, deinit_fn: _, target: _, unwind } then
    match unwind
    when Option::Some(_) then true
    when Option::None then false
    end
  end
end

def slice_control_dependence_walk(ctx: SliceFnCtx, v: Int) -> SliceResult
  var included: Map[String, String] = Map::new()
  var seen: Set[Int] = Set::new()
  var work: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
  var items = 0
  # the seed: the anchor block's own predecessors.
  var pred_rows: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
  match ctx.preds.get(v)
  when Option::Some(rows) then pred_rows = rows.clone()
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  for p in pred_rows do
    if !seen.contains(&p) then
      seen.insert(p)
      work.push(p)
    end
  end
  while work.len() > 0 && items < slice_max_items() do
    items = items + 1
    let b = work[0]
    work.remove(0)
    let term = ctx.f.blocks[b].terminator
    if slice_term_is_conditional(&term) then
      let node_key = slice_term_key(&ctx.name, ctx.f.blocks[b].id.id)
      if !included.contains_key(&node_key) then
        let nspan = slice_span_copy(term.span)
        included.insert(node_key, slice_span_key(&node_key, nspan))
      end
    end
    var b_preds: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
    match ctx.preds.get(b)
    when Option::Some(rows2) then b_preds = rows2.clone()
    when Option::None then ()
    end
    for q in b_preds do
      if !seen.contains(&q) then
        seen.insert(q)
        work.push(q)
      end
    end
  end
  let empty_ext: Set[String] = Set::new()
  slice_result_build(&ctx, &included, &empty_ext)
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The node-anchored BackwardDataflow slice
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The anchor node + the anchored def chains of every value the node reads
# (one shared SliceBack engine — the slice_value machinery seeded at the
# anchor's use sites; a node reading nothing yields the anchor node alone;
# a node with no defs below the reads stops at the parameters/externals
# per the engine's rules).

def slice_backward_node_slice(ctx: SliceFnCtx, v: Int, idx: Int) -> SliceResult
  var back = SliceBack { ctx: ctx.clone(), work: Vec::new(), seen: Set::new(), included: Map::new(), external: Set::new(), items: 0 }
  let block_len = back.ctx.f.blocks[v].statements.len()
  var reads: Vec[Int] = Vec::new()
  var span = Span { file: "", start: 0, end_pos: 0 }
  if idx >= block_len then
    let term = back.ctx.f.blocks[v].terminator
    reads = slice_term_reads(&term)
    span = slice_span_copy(term.span)
  else
    let st = back.ctx.f.blocks[v].statements[idx]
    reads = slice_stmt_reads(st)
    span = slice_span_copy(st.span)
  end
  # the anchor node itself, then one anchored def-chain walk per read.
  slice_back_include(&mut back, v, idx, span)
  for r in reads do
    slice_backward_at(&mut back, v, idx, r)
  end
  slice_result_build(&back.ctx, &back.included, &back.external)
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The local-anchored ForwardDataflow slice
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The forward use slice of ONE local's value: the entry-value chain (the
# value as it enters the first block — a parameter's uses, for example)
# UNION one chain per def site of the local (the def node itself is
# included; the engine follows the def's uses forward until a later def
# kills the chain). One shared SliceFwd engine = one 4096-item budget,
# deterministic FIFO order.

def slice_forward_value_slice(ctx: SliceFnCtx, local: Int) -> SliceResult
  var fwd = SliceFwd { ctx: ctx.clone(), work: Vec::new(), seen: Set::new(), included: Map::new(), external: Set::new(), items: 0 }
  # (a) the value as it enters the entry block.
  let entry_v = slice_block_vec_index(&fwd.ctx, fwd.ctx.f.entry_block.id)
  slice_fwd_push(&mut fwd, entry_v, 0, local)
  # (b) one chain per def site (bare or partial) with the def node itself.
  var bi = 0
  while bi < fwd.ctx.f.blocks.len() do
    let block_len = fwd.ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements.len()
    var si = 0
    while si < block_len do
      let st = fwd.ctx.f.blocks[bi].statements[si]
      let st_defs = slice_stmt_defs(st)
      if st_defs.0 == local || st_defs.1 == local then
        let span = slice_span_copy(st.span)
        slice_fwd_include(&mut fwd, bi, si, span)
        slice_fwd_push(&mut fwd, bi, si + 1, local)
      end
      si = si + 1
    end
    let term = fwd.ctx.f.blocks[bi].terminator
    let term_defs = slice_term_defs(&term)
    if term_defs.0 == local || term_defs.1 == local then
      let tspan = slice_span_copy(term.span)
      slice_fwd_include(&mut fwd, bi, block_len, tspan)
      slice_fwd_push(&mut fwd, bi, block_len + 1, local)
    end
    bi = bi + 1
  end
  slice_fwd_run(&mut fwd)
  slice_result_build(&fwd.ctx, &fwd.included, &fwd.external)
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The typed surface — conversion + per-kind routes
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# The MirSlice view of a slice result (span_keys never cross this
# boundary — presentation-only per the module doc). A result carrying the
# EMPTY marker function key (slice_result_empty — the documented "no
# slice" marker of the four defs, e.g. a def-less ForwardDataflow node)
# is normalized onto the request's function key: an empty Ok slice still
# names its function.
def slice_mir_of_result(fn_key: String, r: SliceResult, kind: MirSliceKind) -> MirSlice
  var fk = r.function_key.clone()
  if fk.len() == 0 then
    fk = fn_key
  end
  MirSlice {
    function_key: fk,
    statements: r.statements.clone(),
    externals: r.external.clone(),
    kind: kind
  }
end

# BackwardDataflow: node anchors slice the node + its reads' def chains;
# local anchors delegate the whole slice_value walk of the local.
def slice_mir_backward(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String, anchor: String) -> Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError]
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::None then
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::FunctionNotFound)
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    if slice_key_marker(&anchor) > 0 then
      match slice_node_anchor_at(&ctx, &anchor)
      when Option::Some(parts) then
        return Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), slice_backward_node_slice(&ctx, parts.0, parts.1), MirSliceKind::BackwardDataflow))
      when Option::None then
        return Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
      end
    else
      match slice_local_anchor_at(&ctx, &anchor)
      when Option::Some(local) then
        return Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), slice_value(mir, fn_key, local), MirSliceKind::BackwardDataflow))
      when Option::None then
        return Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
      end
    end
    # unreachable: every path above returned.
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
  end
end

# ForwardDataflow: node anchors delegate slice_statement (a def-less node —
# asserts, checks, switches — yields the documented empty slice); local
# anchors delegate the forward value slice below.
def slice_mir_forward(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String, anchor: String) -> Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError]
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::None then
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::FunctionNotFound)
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    if slice_key_marker(&anchor) > 0 then
      # validated here (a def-less node — asserts, checks, switches —
      # yields the documented empty slice through slice_statement).
      match slice_node_anchor_at(&ctx, &anchor)
      when Option::Some(_) then
        return Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), slice_statement(mir, fn_key, anchor), MirSliceKind::ForwardDataflow))
      when Option::None then
        return Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
      end
    else
      match slice_local_anchor_at(&ctx, &anchor)
      when Option::Some(local) then
        return Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), slice_forward_value_slice(&ctx, local), MirSliceKind::ForwardDataflow))
      when Option::None then
        return Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
      end
    end
    # unreachable: every path above returned.
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
  end
end

# ControlDependence: a node-key anchor names the block whose reachability
# the walk decides (its block Vec index + the conditional terminators on
# its predecessor chains — see the walk doc).
def slice_mir_control(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String, anchor: String) -> Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError]
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::None then
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::FunctionNotFound)
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    match slice_node_anchor_at(&ctx, &anchor)
    when Option::Some(parts) then
      return Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), slice_control_dependence_walk(&ctx, parts.0), MirSliceKind::ControlDependence))
    when Option::None then
      return Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
    end
    # unreachable: every path above returned.
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
  end
end

# Ownership: the anchor is a §27 local key text (the whole family under
# the local) or a §7 place key text rooted at a local (the anchored place
# and its descendants) — see the walk doc.
def slice_mir_ownership(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String, anchor: String) -> Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError]
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::None then
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::FunctionNotFound)
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    # the root segment: the text up to the first projection character.
    var root_end = 0
    while root_end < anchor.len() do
      let ch = anchor.slice(root_end, root_end + 1)
      if ch == "." || ch == "[" || ch == "*" then
        break
      end
      root_end = root_end + 1
    end
    let root_text = anchor.slice(0, root_end)
    match slice_local_anchor_at(&ctx, &root_text)
    when Option::Some(root) then
      let tail = anchor.slice(root_end, anchor.len())
      return Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), slice_ownership_walk(&mir, &ctx, root, &tail), MirSliceKind::Ownership))
    when Option::None then
      return Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
    end
    # unreachable: every path above returned.
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
  end
end

# Effects: the anchor is a class word; the result is the request function's
# DIRECT §11 row (slice_effect's per-function rows — the class's direct
# sites + their anchored def chains). A function whose summary reaches the
# class only through in-program callees has no DIRECT row: the empty Ok
# slice (the sites live in the callees' rows — documented).
def slice_mir_effects(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String, anchor: String) -> Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError]
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::None then
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::FunctionNotFound)
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    match slice_effect_class_of_anchor(&anchor)
    when Option::Some(class) then
      let rows = slice_effect(mir, class)
      var row: Option[SliceResult] = Option::None
      for r in rows do
        if r.function_key == ctx.name then
          row = Option::Some(r.clone())
          break
        end
      end
      match row
      when Option::Some(res) then
        return Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), res.clone(), MirSliceKind::Effects))
      when Option::None then
        return Result::Ok(MirSlice {
          function_key: ctx.name.clone(),
          statements: Vec::new(),
          externals: Vec::new(),
          kind: MirSliceKind::Effects
        })
      end
    when Option::None then
      return Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
    end
    # unreachable: every path above returned.
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
  end
end

# Failure: the anchor is the node key of the failing site; the result is
# the failure trace + the anchored def chains of its reads — the exact
# slice_failure machinery over the direct node anchor.
def slice_mir_failure(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String, anchor: String) -> Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError]
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::None then
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::FunctionNotFound)
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    match slice_node_anchor_at(&ctx, &anchor)
    when Option::Some(parts) then
      return Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), slice_failure_node_slice(&ctx, parts.0, parts.1), MirSliceKind::Failure))
    when Option::None then
      return Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
    end
    # unreachable: every path above returned.
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::AnchorNotFound)
  end
end

# ReturnValue: the backward slice of the return local — local 0, the "_ret"
# place of start_function's convention (MirReturn terminators read it, so
# slice_value resolves one def chain per return site). The anchor text is
# ignored (documented). A bodyless function (no locals) yields the empty
# Ok slice.
def slice_mir_return(mir: MirProgram, fn_key: String) -> Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError]
  match slice_fn_find(mir, fn_key.clone())
  when Option::None then
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::FunctionNotFound)
  when Option::Some(ctx) then
    if ctx.f.locals.len() <= 0 then
      return Result::Ok(MirSlice {
        function_key: ctx.name.clone(),
        statements: Vec::new(),
        externals: Vec::new(),
        kind: MirSliceKind::ReturnValue
      })
    end
    let r = slice_value(mir, fn_key, 0)
    Result::Ok(slice_mir_of_result(fn_key.clone(), r, MirSliceKind::ReturnValue))
  end
end

# The ONE typed slicing entry — routes the request per kind onto the
# engines above; see the section doc for the anchor grammar and the error
# mapping.
pub def mir_slice(program: Option[MirProgram], request: MirSliceRequest) -> Result[MirSlice, MirSliceError]
  match program
  when Option::None then
    Result::Err(MirSliceError::MirProgramUnavailable)
  when Option::Some(mir) then
    match request.kind
    when MirSliceKind::BackwardDataflow then slice_mir_backward(mir, request.function_key.clone(), request.anchor.clone())
    when MirSliceKind::ForwardDataflow then slice_mir_forward(mir, request.function_key.clone(), request.anchor.clone())
    when MirSliceKind::ControlDependence then slice_mir_control(mir, request.function_key.clone(), request.anchor.clone())
    when MirSliceKind::Ownership then slice_mir_ownership(mir, request.function_key.clone(), request.anchor.clone())
    when MirSliceKind::Effects then slice_mir_effects(mir, request.function_key.clone(), request.anchor.clone())
    when MirSliceKind::Failure then slice_mir_failure(mir, request.function_key.clone(), request.anchor.clone())
    when MirSliceKind::ReturnValue then slice_mir_return(mir, request.function_key.clone())
    end
  end
end
